        <h1>LeetCode 3876: Construct Uniform Parity Array II (C++)</h1>
        <div class="problem-description">
            <p><strong>Problem:</strong>
                You are given an array nums1 of n distinct integers. Construct another array nums2 of length n such
                that all elements in nums2 are either odd or even. For each index i, choose exactly one of the
                following options, in any order: nums2[i] = nums1[i], or nums2[i] = nums1[i] - nums1[j] for an index
                j != i, such that nums1[i] - nums1[j] &gt;= 1. Return true if it is possible to construct nums2;
                otherwise, return false.
            </p>
            <p><strong>Example 1:</strong>
                Input: nums1 = [1,4,7]<br>
                Output: true<br>
                Explanation: Choose nums2 = [1,3,7] by keeping 1, subtracting 1 from 4, and keeping 7. All elements
                are odd.
            </p>
            <p><strong>Example 2:</strong>
                Input: nums1 = [2,3]<br>
                Output: false<br>
                Explanation: It is not possible to construct nums2 such that all elements have the same parity.
            </p>
            <p><strong>Example 3:</strong>
                Input: nums1 = [4,6]<br>
                Output: true<br>
                Explanation: Keep both values to get nums2 = [4,6]. All elements are even.
            </p>
            <p><strong>Constraints:</strong>
                1 &lt;= n == nums1.length &lt;= 10<sup>5</sup>, 1 &lt;= nums1[i] &lt;= 10<sup>9</sup>, and nums1
                consists
                of distinct integers.
            </p>
        </div>
        <div class="code-container">
            <button class="copy-button" onclick="copyCode(this)">Copy Code</button>
            <pre><code class="language-cpp">class Solution {
public:
	bool uniformArray(vector&lt;int&gt;&amp; nums) {
		int minOdd = INT_MAX;
		bool hasOdd = false;
		for (int value : nums) {
			if (value % 2) {
				hasOdd = true;
				minOdd = min(minOdd, value);
			}
		}
		if (!hasOdd)
			return true;
		for (int value : nums) {
			if (value % 2 == 0 &amp;&amp; value &lt; minOdd)
				return false;
		}
		return true;
	}
};</code></pre>
